      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60e65f577ae9d0492b0f2a75|full_name} It's insane that we have to figure out which of these random checks is the source of the failure because the log message says nothing but \"oops something broke!\" to even file a bug report. They could just as easily have designed these checks to set a flag server-side and continue. Instead we have this stupid design where we both have an opaque and indecipherable checking infrastructure but the responsibility is also on us to figure out what's wrong with it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
